course: dictionary
lesson: 5329
title: One word, many keys
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word key has more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one is meant. «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window» is about a small metal key that opens a lock. Ask yourself: what is the key used for in this sentence?
explain: Key can also mean a button you press, like the keys on a keyboard or the black and white keys on a piano. «Riddles play with double meanings: "keys" can open locks, or be the black and white keys of a piano» shows a writer using both meanings on purpose, and the reader must switch between them.
explain: Key can also mean the most important thing. A key word carries the main meaning of a sentence, and the key to a puzzle is the thing that helps you solve it. Check the words around key: if the sentence is about a map, a lock or a piano, that tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Key has many meanings, so always check the context to find the right one.
fact: A key can be a small metal tool that opens a lock, or a button on a keyboard.
fact: On a piano, the keys are the black and white bars you press, and a piano has 88 keys.
fact: The key on a map tells you what each picture, colour or sign means.
fact: A key word is the most important word in a text, and to key in means to type.
exercise: «If you lose your key, do not climb in through a window.» What is a key in this sentence? | A sign on a map | *A small metal tool that opens a lock | A button on a keyboard | A word that means very important
exercise: On a map, what does the key tell you? | Who lives in each house | How far it is to the sea | *What each picture, colour or sign means | The name of the town
exercise: What is a key word in a text? | A word that is always spelled wrong | *The most important word that carries the main meaning | A word from another language | A word with a silent letter
test: How many keys does a piano have? | *88 | 12 | 52 | 100
test: «Riddles play with double meanings: "keys" can open locks, or be the black and white keys of a piano.» What two meanings of key does this sentence show? | *Keys that open locks and keys on a piano | Keys that are hot and keys that are cold | Keys that fly and keys that swim
exam: Mia says, «The key to the riddle is the piano.» In this sentence, what does key mean? | *The thing that helps you solve or understand something | A button on a keyboard | A sign on a map | A small metal tool that opens a lock
